{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VXFsKC68qUkmEPo9n4icTn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\t# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n3\t# manigot agent reference template — copy me to make a real agent\n4\t# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n5\t# Copy this file to `docs/agents/<name>.md` (a project agent — it overrides a\n6\t# global agent of the same name) or `agents/<name>.md` (a global agent in the\n7\t# manigot checkout) and rename `name:` to match the filename. Every key is\n8\t# optional; a key is enforced only when it is actually present in the live file.\n9\t# Comments like this one are explanatory — delete them from your copy.\n10\t#\n11\t# Two keys in this template are part of the DESIGNED guardrail surface and are\n12\t# NOT YET ENFORCED — keep them commented out until they land: `deny:` (command\n13\t# deny-list) and `network:` (session network isolation). Everything else below\n14\t# is enforced today.\n15\t\n16\t# ── Identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17\t# Shown as @<name> in sessions, in `mg agents` (and the TUI picker) and in\n18\t# @mention autocomplete. Must match the filename.\n19\tname: example-agent\n20\t# One line, shown by `mg agents` / the TUI picker. No trailing period.\n21\tdescription: Reference agent showing every manigot frontmatter key and guardrail.\n22\t\n23\t# ── Tool surface — Claude Code ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n24\t# Comma-separated allowlist enforced by Claude Code. Read-only agents keep the\n25\t# read surface (Read, Grep, Glob); full agents add Write, Edit, Bash.\n26\t# OpenCode strips this key at conversion (it uses a map schema) and enforces\n27\t# the `permission:` block below instead.\n28\ttools: Read, Grep, Glob\n29\t\n30\t# ── Git mount — the hard filesystem boundary (both CLIs) ────────────────────\n31\t# true  → the job's git-common-dir is mounted writable; the agent may commit.\n32\t# false → it is mounted READ-ONLY (with GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0): the agent\n33\t#         physically cannot touch git metadata — the hard boundary behind the\n34\t#         soft git shim. The default (no marker / unknown value) is true, so a\n35\t#         committing agent is never broken by a missing marker.\n36\tcommit: false\n37\t\n38\t# ── OpenCode permission block — deny/allow, last-match-wins ─────────────────\n39\t# Passed through manigot's OpenCode conversion verbatim. Claude Code ignores it\n40\t# (covered by `tools:` and the git shim). Denies must be listed AFTER allows.\n41\t# The built-in read-only agents express their restriction with exactly this\n42\t# key: allow only the agent's own report file and the read-only git commands,\n43\t# deny everything else (task/webfetch/websearch/question, destructive git).\n44\tpermission:\n45\t  edit:\n46\t    \"*\": deny\n47\t    \"docs/jobs/**/verdict.md\": allow\n48\t  bash:\n49\t    \"*\": deny\n50\t    \"git add *\": allow\n51\t    \"git commit *\": allow\n52\t    \"git diff *\": allow\n53\t    \"git log *\": allow\n54\t    \"git show *\": allow\n55\t    \"git status *\": allow\n56\t    \"git rev-parse *\": allow\n57\t    \"git branch --show-current\": allow\n58\t    \"git branch --show-current *\": allow\n59\t    \"git worktree*\": deny\n60\t    \"git branch -d*\": deny\n61\t    \"git branch -D*\": deny\n62\t    \"git branch --delete*\": deny\n63\t    \"git branch --move*\": deny\n64\t    \"git branch --copy*\": deny\n65\t    \"git reset*\": deny\n66\t    \"git clean*\": deny\n67\t    \"git gc*\": deny\n68\t    \"git prune*\": deny\n69\t    \"git reflog*\": deny\n70\t    \"git push*\": deny\n71\t    \"git fetch*\": deny\n72\t    \"git pull*\": deny\n73\t    \"git checkout*\": deny\n74\t    \"git switch*\": deny\n75\t    \"git restore*\": deny\n76\t    \"git stash*\": deny\n77\t    \"git remote*\": deny\n78\t    \"git tag -d*\": deny\n79\t    \"git update-ref*\": deny\n80\t  task: deny\n81\t  webfetch: deny\n82\t  websearch: deny\n83\t  question: deny\n84\t\n85\t# ── Command deny-list — DESIGNED, NOT YET ENFORCED ───────────────────────────\n86\t# OpenCode-style glob patterns of commands this agent must never run. When it\n87\t# lands, each entry is enforced two ways: merged into the `permission.bash`\n88\t# denies above under OpenCode, and a PATH-first shim (the git-shim pattern)\n89\t# that fails with a clear message under both CLIs. Example — the session image\n90\t# has no virtualenv, so stop the agent burning turns on `command not found`:\n91\t# deny:\n92\t#   - \"venv*\"\n93\t#   - \"pyvenv*\"\n94\t#   - \"virtualenv*\"\n95\t#   - \"python -m venv*\"\n96\t#   - \"python3 -m venv*\"\n97\t\n98\t# ── Network isolation — DESIGNED, NOT YET ENFORCED ───────────────────────────\n99\t# Intended mapping to the docker `--network` flag for the session:\n100\t#   none     → no network at all (the strongest isolation)\n101\t#   loopback → localhost only\n102\t#   bridge   → today's default: full egress\n103\t# network: none\n104\t---\n105\t\n106\tYou are a reference agent — this file is a template, not a live agent. Copy it\n107\tto `docs/agents/<name>.md` and rewrite this body for the role you want.\n108\t\n109\t## Role\n110\t\n111\tOne paragraph: who you are and what job you do.\n112\t\n113\t## Before starting (job sessions)\n114\t\n115\t1. Read `brief.md` — what the job is about, and its `branch:` field.\n116\t2. Read `tasks.md` — the full task list.\n117\t3. Check the branch: `git branch --show-current`. The mounted workspace is the\n118\t   job's own worktree, always on the job branch — no `git checkout` needed. If\n119\t   the branch differs from `brief.md`, stop and report back.\n120\t\n121\t## Constraints and guardrails\n122\t\n123\t- Keep changes scoped to the task. When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess.\n124\t- Never commit `.env` or any file containing credentials.\n125\t- Never touch files outside the job's `docs/` unless the task requires it.\n126\t- The session git shim restricts git to reading history and making commits\n127\t  (`git add`, `git commit`, `git log`, `git diff`, `git show`, `git status`,\n128\t  ...) — worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, stash,\n129\t  merge, rebase, ... are refused.\n130\t- When running non-interactively (`mg jdi` / `--print`), if you cannot proceed\n131\t  without a human decision, stop and print a line starting with exactly\n132\t  `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT:` followed by a one-sentence reason, and make no further\n133\t  changes.\n134\t\n135\t## Hard rules\n136\t\n137\t- Do not push\n138\t- Do not merge\n139\t- Do not touch any other branch\n140\t- Do not install packages without asking first\n141\t- [add your own]\n142\t\n143\t## (Reference) manigot guardrails at a glance\n144\t\n145\t| Guardrail | Enforced today | Layer |\n146\t|---|---|---|\n147\t| `tools:` allowlist | Claude Code | CLI tool schema |\n148\t| `permission:` block | OpenCode | CLI permission config, last-match-wins |\n149\t| `commit: false` → read-only gitdir | both CLIs | Docker `:ro` mount (+ `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`) |\n150\t| git shim (read + commit only) | both CLIs | PATH-first shim — soft layer |\n151\t| `hooks/` + other jobs' worktree gitdirs read-only | both CLIs | Docker `:ro` overlay mounts (job sessions) |\n152\t| `.env` / `.env.*` shadowed to `/dev/null` | both CLIs | Docker bind mount |\n153\t| profile credentials pinned per profile | both CLIs | session launcher env |\n154\t| `shot` only for committing agents | both CLIs | `MANIGOT_AGENT_COMMITS` guard + permission blocks |\n155\t| `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT:` marker | `mg jdi` / `--print` | orchestrate state machine |\n156\t| sweep-commit of session leftovers | job-worktree sessions | session launcher |\n157\t| `deny:` command deny-list | NOT YET | designed (OpenCode permission + PATH shim) |\n158\t| `network:` session isolation | NOT YET | designed (docker `--network`) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e2afcf5-7fc0-4a90-a6a6-e82e43a08449","uuid":"05333c33-d4b1-4724-9852-c0d6677b6075","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:47:56.417Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/agent-template.md","content":"---\n# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# manigot agent reference template — copy me to make a real agent\n# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# Copy this file to `docs/agents/<name>.md` (a project agent — it overrides a\n# global agent of the same name) or `agents/<name>.md` (a global agent in the\n# manigot checkout) and rename `name:` to match the filename. Every key is\n# optional; a key is enforced only when it is actually present in the live file.\n# Comments like this one are explanatory — delete them from your copy.\n#\n# Two keys in this template are part of the DESIGNED guardrail surface and are\n# NOT YET ENFORCED — keep them commented out until they land: `deny:` (command\n# deny-list) and `network:` (session network isolation). Everything else below\n# is enforced today.\n\n# ── Identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Shown as @<name> in sessions, in `mg agents` (and the TUI picker) and in\n# @mention autocomplete. Must match the filename.\nname: example-agent\n# One line, shown by `mg agents` / the TUI picker. No trailing period.\ndescription: Reference agent showing every manigot frontmatter key and guardrail.\n\n# ── Tool surface — Claude Code ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Comma-separated allowlist enforced by Claude Code. Read-only agents keep the\n# read surface (Read, Grep, Glob); full agents add Write, Edit, Bash.\n# OpenCode strips this key at conversion (it uses a map schema) and enforces\n# the `permission:` block below instead.\ntools: Read, Grep, Glob\n\n# ── Git mount — the hard filesystem boundary (both CLIs) ────────────────────\n# true  → the job's git-common-dir is mounted writable; the agent may commit.\n# false → it is mounted READ-ONLY (with GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0): the agent\n#         physically cannot touch git metadata — the hard boundary behind the\n#         soft git shim. The default (no marker / unknown value) is true, so a\n#         committing agent is never broken by a missing marker.\ncommit: false\n\n# ── OpenCode permission block — deny/allow, last-match-wins ─────────────────\n# Passed through manigot's OpenCode conversion verbatim. Claude Code ignores it\n# (covered by `tools:` and the git shim). Denies must be listed AFTER allows.\n# The built-in read-only agents express their restriction with exactly this\n# key: allow only the agent's own report file and the read-only git commands,\n# deny everything else (task/webfetch/websearch/question, destructive git).\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": deny\n    \"docs/jobs/**/verdict.md\": allow\n  bash:\n    \"*\": deny\n    \"git add *\": allow\n    \"git commit *\": allow\n    \"git diff *\": allow\n    \"git log *\": allow\n    \"git show *\": allow\n    \"git status *\": allow\n    \"git rev-parse *\": allow\n    \"git branch --show-current\": allow\n    \"git branch --show-current *\": allow\n    \"git worktree*\": deny\n    \"git branch -d*\": deny\n    \"git branch -D*\": deny\n    \"git branch --delete*\": deny\n    \"git branch --move*\": deny\n    \"git branch --copy*\": deny\n    \"git reset*\": deny\n    \"git clean*\": deny\n    \"git gc*\": deny\n    \"git prune*\": deny\n    \"git reflog*\": deny\n    \"git push*\": deny\n    \"git fetch*\": deny\n    \"git pull*\": deny\n    \"git checkout*\": deny\n    \"git switch*\": deny\n    \"git restore*\": deny\n    \"git stash*\": deny\n    \"git remote*\": deny\n    \"git tag -d*\": deny\n    \"git update-ref*\": deny\n  task: deny\n  webfetch: deny\n  websearch: deny\n  question: deny\n\n# ── Command deny-list — DESIGNED, NOT YET ENFORCED ───────────────────────────\n# OpenCode-style glob patterns of commands this agent must never run. When it\n# lands, each entry is enforced two ways: merged into the `permission.bash`\n# denies above under OpenCode, and a PATH-first shim (the git-shim pattern)\n# that fails with a clear message under both CLIs. Example — the session image\n# has no virtualenv, so stop the agent burning turns on `command not found`:\n# deny:\n#   - \"venv*\"\n#   - \"pyvenv*\"\n#   - \"virtualenv*\"\n#   - \"python -m venv*\"\n#   - \"python3 -m venv*\"\n\n# ── Network isolation — DESIGNED, NOT YET ENFORCED ───────────────────────────\n# Intended mapping to the docker `--network` flag for the session:\n#   none     → no network at all (the strongest isolation)\n#   loopback → localhost only\n#   bridge   → today's default: full egress\n# network: none\n---\n\nYou are a reference agent — this file is a template, not a live agent. Copy it\nto `docs/agents/<name>.md` and rewrite this body for the role you want.\n\n## Role\n\nOne paragraph: who you are and what job you do.\n\n## Before starting (job sessions)\n\n1. Read `brief.md` — what the job is about, and its `branch:` field.\n2. Read `tasks.md` — the full task list.\n3. Check the branch: `git branch --show-current`. The mounted workspace is the\n   job's own worktree, always on the job branch — no `git checkout` needed. If\n   the branch differs from `brief.md`, stop and report back.\n\n## Constraints and guardrails\n\n- Keep changes scoped to the task. When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess.\n- Never commit `.env` or any file containing credentials.\n- Never touch files outside the job's `docs/` unless the task requires it.\n- The session git shim restricts git to reading history and making commits\n  (`git add`, `git commit`, `git log`, `git diff`, `git show`, `git status`,\n  ...) — worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, stash,\n  merge, rebase, ... are refused.\n- When running non-interactively (`mg jdi` / `--print`), if you cannot proceed\n  without a human decision, stop and print a line starting with exactly\n  `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT:` followed by a one-sentence reason, and make no further\n  changes.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- Do not push\n- Do not merge\n- Do not touch any other branch\n- Do not install packages without asking first\n- [add your own]\n\n## (Reference) manigot guardrails at a glance\n\n| Guardrail | Enforced today | Layer |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tools:` allowlist | Claude Code | CLI tool schema |\n| `permission:` block | OpenCode | CLI permission config, last-match-wins |\n| `commit: false` → read-only gitdir | both CLIs | Docker `:ro` mount (+ `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`) |\n| git shim (read + commit only) | both CLIs | PATH-first shim — soft layer |\n| `hooks/` + other jobs' worktree gitdirs read-only | both CLIs | Docker `:ro` overlay mounts (job sessions) |\n| `.env` / `.env.*` shadowed to `/dev/null` | both CLIs | Docker bind mount |\n| profile credentials pinned per profile | both CLIs | session launcher env |\n| `shot` only for committing agents | both CLIs | `MANIGOT_AGENT_COMMITS` guard + permission blocks |\n| `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT:` marker | `mg jdi` / `--print` | orchestrate state machine |\n| sweep-commit of session leftovers | job-worktree sessions | session launcher |\n| `deny:` command deny-list | NOT YET | designed (OpenCode permission + PATH shim) |\n| `network:` session isolation | NOT YET | designed (docker `--network`) |","numLines":158,"startLine":1,"totalLines":158}}}
