{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MBpfoKvFabrjM6a7MibgTX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Brief: mcp support\n2\t\n3\tstatus: open\n4\ttype: feature\n5\tid: gradually\n6\tbranch: feature/gradually_mcp-support\n7\tdate: 2026-08-31\n8\tauthor: Leander Muskalla\n9\t\n10\t## What\n11\t\n12\tA global+project delivery mechanism for MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers,\n13\tmodeled directly on how manigot already delivers agents and skills, plus\n14\tContext7 (a hosted documentation-lookup MCP server) as the first server\n15\tshipped through it.\n16\t\n17\t- **Directory layout**: `mcp/<name>.json` in the checkout (global, delivered\n18\t  to every session), overridable/extendable per project via\n19\t  `docs/mcp/<name>.json` (same filename → project replaces global entirely;\n20\t  new filename → project adds a server). This mirrors `agents/` +\n21\t  `docs/agents/` and `skills/` + `docs/skills/` exactly.\n22\t- **Canonical per-server schema**, CLI-agnostic (manigot's own shape, not\n23\t  either CLI's native one):\n24\t  ```json\n25\t  { \"type\": \"http\", \"url\": \"...\", \"headers\": { \"SOME_KEY\": \"$SOME_KEY\" } }\n26\t  ```\n27\t  or for a locally-spawned server:\n28\t  ```json\n29\t  { \"type\": \"stdio\", \"command\": \"...\", \"args\": [...], \"env\": { \"SOME_KEY\": \"$SOME_KEY\" } }\n30\t  ```\n31\t  `$VARNAME` in any string value references a manigot `.env` key — servers\n32\t  never carry a literal secret in a committed file.\n33\t- **First shipped server**: `mcp/context7.json`, hosted HTTP only —\n34\t  `https://mcp.context7.com/mcp`, with an optional `CONTEXT7_API_KEY`\n35\t  (`.env` key, works unauthenticated at a lower rate limit). No local\n36\t  process, no new image dependency.\n37\t- **Merge + delivery**: at session launch, global + project server files are\n38\t  merged (project wins by filename), converted into each CLI's native\n39\t  config shape, and mounted read-only into the container — Claude Code as a\n40\t  generated `.mcp.json` at the workspace root (shadowing any real project\n41\t  `.mcp.json`, the same way `.env` files are already shadow-mounted),\n42\t  OpenCode folded into its existing `opencode.json` (which today only\n43\t  carries the resolved model). No servers configured anywhere → nothing\n44\t  generated, nothing mounted — identical behavior to today.\n45\t\n46\t## Why\n47\t\n48\tThere's currently no way to give every manigot session access to reusable\n49\texternal tools/knowledge sources via MCP — each agent works from what it\n50\talready knows plus whatever's in the repo. Context7 gives agents live,\n51\tversion-accurate library documentation instead of guessing from training\n52\tdata; the general mechanism means the next MCP server (or a project's own)\n53\tis a JSON file drop-in, not a code change.\n54\t\n55\t## Out of scope\n56\t\n57\t- `mg host` sessions: host mode deliberately never writes into the user's\n58\t  own real Claude Code / OpenCode config (same reason `OPENCODE_MODEL` and\n59\t  `OPENCODE_THEME` are already excluded there — see `host.go`). MCP servers\n60\t  in host mode would need to already be configured in the user's own CLI\n61\t  config; not this job's problem to solve.\n62\t- Any `mg mcp` CLI surface (add/rm/list) — start file-based only, the same\n63\t  way `agents/`/`skills/` shipped before `mg agents` existed.\n64\t- Shipping a second (stdio-based) server — the schema must support `type:\n65\t  \"stdio\"` so the mechanism isn't Context7-special-cased, but only Context7\n66\t  ships in this job.\n67\t- Relying on either CLI's own `${VAR}`-style config-file env expansion —\n68\t  manigot resolves `$VARNAME` itself, host-side, into the generated config\n69\t  (OpenCode's `{env:VAR}` form is confirmed elsewhere in this codebase\n70\t  already, but Claude Code's equivalent isn't, so don't depend on it for\n71\t  either CLI — keep both paths uniform and independently verified).\n72\t\n73\t## Notes\n74\t\n75\t- Reference implementation for the merge/convert step:\n76\t  `src/internal/session/agentconv.go` and `skillconv.go` (list + convert +\n77\t  temp-dir staging, cleaned up via the invocation's `Cleanup` hook).\n78\t- Reference implementation for the shadow-mount-over-a-real-file pattern:\n79\t  `BuildDockerInvocation`'s `.env` shadow-mount block in\n80\t  `src/internal/session/docker.go`.\n81\t- The OpenCode `opencode.json` write currently lives in `scripts/entrypoint.sh`\n82\t  (model only, guarded by \"only if the file doesn't already exist\" — see\n83\t  around line 84). That guard can't compose a second, independently-generated\n84\t  piece of content into the same file, so generating the complete\n85\t  `opencode.json` (model + mcp) needs to move host-side into Go, mounted in\n86\t  the same way agents/skills already are. `entrypoint.sh`'s `tui.json`\n87\t  (theme) write is untouched — it's a separate file with nothing to merge.\n88\t- Because `entrypoint.sh` runs Claude Code with\n89\t  `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, the normal \"trust this MCP server?\"\n90\t  prompt never appears for the generated `.mcp.json` — the server is trusted\n91\t  automatically, same as every other tool in this mode. Not new risk\n92\t  surface, but `@security` should look at it explicitly given it's a\n93\t  network-facing server.\n94\t- `agents/*.md`, `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md`, and this repo's own\n95\t  `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (root) all describe the agents/skills mechanism in\n96\t  parallel prose today — the new `mcp/` mechanism needs the same treatment\n97\t  in all three, not just code. Treat this as a required task, not cleanup.\n98\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ff35466-1740-4190-9c53-6ab704f13a39","uuid":"da91349f-438a-46bc-b4ce-1d459f8a9b91","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:50:29.543Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/gradually_mcp-support/brief.md","content":"# Brief: mcp support\n\nstatus: open\ntype: feature\nid: gradually\nbranch: feature/gradually_mcp-support\ndate: 2026-08-31\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nA global+project delivery mechanism for MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers,\nmodeled directly on how manigot already delivers agents and skills, plus\nContext7 (a hosted documentation-lookup MCP server) as the first server\nshipped through it.\n\n- **Directory layout**: `mcp/<name>.json` in the checkout (global, delivered\n  to every session), overridable/extendable per project via\n  `docs/mcp/<name>.json` (same filename → project replaces global entirely;\n  new filename → project adds a server). This mirrors `agents/` +\n  `docs/agents/` and `skills/` + `docs/skills/` exactly.\n- **Canonical per-server schema**, CLI-agnostic (manigot's own shape, not\n  either CLI's native one):\n  ```json\n  { \"type\": \"http\", \"url\": \"...\", \"headers\": { \"SOME_KEY\": \"$SOME_KEY\" } }\n  ```\n  or for a locally-spawned server:\n  ```json\n  { \"type\": \"stdio\", \"command\": \"...\", \"args\": [...], \"env\": { \"SOME_KEY\": \"$SOME_KEY\" } }\n  ```\n  `$VARNAME` in any string value references a manigot `.env` key — servers\n  never carry a literal secret in a committed file.\n- **First shipped server**: `mcp/context7.json`, hosted HTTP only —\n  `https://mcp.context7.com/mcp`, with an optional `CONTEXT7_API_KEY`\n  (`.env` key, works unauthenticated at a lower rate limit). No local\n  process, no new image dependency.\n- **Merge + delivery**: at session launch, global + project server files are\n  merged (project wins by filename), converted into each CLI's native\n  config shape, and mounted read-only into the container — Claude Code as a\n  generated `.mcp.json` at the workspace root (shadowing any real project\n  `.mcp.json`, the same way `.env` files are already shadow-mounted),\n  OpenCode folded into its existing `opencode.json` (which today only\n  carries the resolved model). No servers configured anywhere → nothing\n  generated, nothing mounted — identical behavior to today.\n\n## Why\n\nThere's currently no way to give every manigot session access to reusable\nexternal tools/knowledge sources via MCP — each agent works from what it\nalready knows plus whatever's in the repo. Context7 gives agents live,\nversion-accurate library documentation instead of guessing from training\ndata; the general mechanism means the next MCP server (or a project's own)\nis a JSON file drop-in, not a code change.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- `mg host` sessions: host mode deliberately never writes into the user's\n  own real Claude Code / OpenCode config (same reason `OPENCODE_MODEL` and\n  `OPENCODE_THEME` are already excluded there — see `host.go`). MCP servers\n  in host mode would need to already be configured in the user's own CLI\n  config; not this job's problem to solve.\n- Any `mg mcp` CLI surface (add/rm/list) — start file-based only, the same\n  way `agents/`/`skills/` shipped before `mg agents` existed.\n- Shipping a second (stdio-based) server — the schema must support `type:\n  \"stdio\"` so the mechanism isn't Context7-special-cased, but only Context7\n  ships in this job.\n- Relying on either CLI's own `${VAR}`-style config-file env expansion —\n  manigot resolves `$VARNAME` itself, host-side, into the generated config\n  (OpenCode's `{env:VAR}` form is confirmed elsewhere in this codebase\n  already, but Claude Code's equivalent isn't, so don't depend on it for\n  either CLI — keep both paths uniform and independently verified).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Reference implementation for the merge/convert step:\n  `src/internal/session/agentconv.go` and `skillconv.go` (list + convert +\n  temp-dir staging, cleaned up via the invocation's `Cleanup` hook).\n- Reference implementation for the shadow-mount-over-a-real-file pattern:\n  `BuildDockerInvocation`'s `.env` shadow-mount block in\n  `src/internal/session/docker.go`.\n- The OpenCode `opencode.json` write currently lives in `scripts/entrypoint.sh`\n  (model only, guarded by \"only if the file doesn't already exist\" — see\n  around line 84). That guard can't compose a second, independently-generated\n  piece of content into the same file, so generating the complete\n  `opencode.json` (model + mcp) needs to move host-side into Go, mounted in\n  the same way agents/skills already are. `entrypoint.sh`'s `tui.json`\n  (theme) write is untouched — it's a separate file with nothing to merge.\n- Because `entrypoint.sh` runs Claude Code with\n  `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, the normal \"trust this MCP server?\"\n  prompt never appears for the generated `.mcp.json` — the server is trusted\n  automatically, same as every other tool in this mode. Not new risk\n  surface, but `@security` should look at it explicitly given it's a\n  network-facing server.\n- `agents/*.md`, `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md`, and this repo's own\n  `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (root) all describe the agents/skills mechanism in\n  parallel prose today — the new `mcp/` mechanism needs the same treatment\n  in all three, not just code. Treat this as a required task, not cleanup.\n","numLines":98,"startLine":1,"totalLines":98}}}
